            <ArticleTitle>A review of over three decades of research on cat-human and human-cat interactions and relationships.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>297-304</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0376-6357(16)30322-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.beproc.2017.01.008</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This review article covers research conducted over the last three decades on cat-human and human-cat interactions and relationships, especially from an ethological point of view. It includes findings on cat-cat and cat-human communication, cat personalities and cat-owner personalities, the effects of cats on humans, and problems caused by cats.</AbstractText>
